|~ What is declared under `::tag`, the kind of a tag name: the refusal
   of its constructor, and the verbs that live on a tag name, the
   comparisons of tag names, which compare them by their names in the one
   order, `manifest` and `runLaws`. ~|

:tag/construct
  |~~ Reads a tag name as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/PayloadNotTagError
  |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
      tag is read by `type`.
      ~(
        ::tag:k
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::tag/PayloadNotTagError ::keyword]
       )
  ~~|

:tag/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the tag the call
      gives.

      ~(::b | gt ::a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gt/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The than is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gt/greater
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the tag
      the call gives.

      ~(::b | gte ::b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gte/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The than is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gte/atLeast
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the tag the call
      gives.

      ~(::a | lt ::b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lt/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The than is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lt/less
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      tag the call gives.

      ~(::a | lte ::a | eq true)
      ~(::a | lte ::b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lte/than/NotTagError
  |~~ The than is a tag name. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lte/atMost
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/manifest
  |~~ Asked of a noun, answers the set of the nodes declared one name
      under it, each by its address: ::snippet~(::number | manifest)
      the verbs and the refusals of numbers, ::snippet~(::qlang |
      manifest) the chapters of the language. The kinds of the scope
      `kinds` lists, and what the reader declared `env`; what one node
      holds the axes read, `::vec/count | source`, `| doc`, `| doc |
      laws`.

      ~(::number | manifest | has ::number/add)
      ~(::qlang | manifest | has ::qlang/values)
      ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box | manifest | eq #[::Box/area])

      `manifest` is asked of a noun, a tag name in the subject
      position.

      ~(
        5 | manifest
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError ::number]
       )
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/manifest/names
  |~~ The addresses of the names declared one name under the noun. ~~|
  ::set

:tag/runLaws
  |~~ The results of the laws of the page of the declaration the tag
      name reads, a verb by its address among them, one `{:law :says
      :actual :ok :error}` per law, `:says` the caption of the claim the
      law proves. A keyword after it runs the laws of the member the
      name holds under it, a concept of the language among them.

      ~(::number/add | runLaws | first | /ok | eq true)
      ~(::qlang | runLaws :values | every ~(/ok))
      ~(::number/add | runLaws * /ok | distinct | eq #[true])
      ~(::number/gt | runLaws | count | gte 1)
      ~(42 | runLaws !| /addresses | eq #[::keyword/runLaws ::tag/runLaws])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/runLaws/anchor
  |~~ The anchor within the page, null when it gives none. ~~|
  ~(at 0)

:tag/runLaws/anchor/NotKeywordOrNullError
  |~~ The anchor is a keyword or null. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword ::null)

:tag/runLaws/results
  |~~ One result for each law: the law, its claim, what it answered and whether it held. ~~|
  ::vec
